5. the handoff path for the auditor: /tmp/ops-sync-d78b3e/handoff/audit.md.

Do not run `make`, do not run the test suite, and do not modify the kit. Finish by printing the absolute path of the plan you wrote.

You are the independent reviewer (Phase 3) for the OPS-SYNC S-24 cycle. Your input is /tmp/ops-sync-d78b3e/handoff/operator.log.

Poll for the completed log: run a bash loop until the file exists AND contains the line `status=complete` (up to 180 seconds, checking every 3 seconds). If it never completes, stop and report that.

Read the log in full, then read /tmp/ops-sync-d78b3e/handoff/plan.md and the compiled record at /tmp/ops-sync-d78b3e/state/sprint-report.json. Do not rerun `make test`, and do not modify any file.

Write /tmp/ops-sync-d78b3e/handoff/audit.md with:
1. your verdict, PASS or REVIEW, for the sprint verification;
2. whether the compiled record contains both the scoping and verification status reports, naming them;
3. whether the record's build_host values are consistent with the Build-host context sections in plan.md and operator.log;
4. the record's relay status, quoted verbatim;
5. one sentence on whether the audit trail is complete enough for the sprint to close.

Do not modify the kit, the handoff artifacts, or the record. Finish by printing the audit path.
